# Gotchas only

A gotcha is a claim/evidence pair that passes all four: same nameable fact, evidence runs AGAINST the claim, material to an element/procedure/credibility/damages, and both quotes are in the pulled text. A model pass without those four completed steps does not ship. When a pair is ambiguous, suppress it.

Related documents that show a defect about the same subject often SUPPORT a denial. That is not a gotcha. Shared topic or person is not the same fact.

Do not hardcode practice-area phrases. Types are only: factual contradiction, chronology inconsistency, material omission, procedural/foundational, admission against interest.

Risk scores from verified findings only — never document type or title.
